<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan Telecom rises 7.54 percent.</title>
<headline>Pakistan Telecom rises 7.54 percent.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Pakistan Telecommunications Company Ltd (PTCL) soared 2.15 rupees, or 7.54 percent, to 30.65 on Sunday on news the government might double the line rent for telephones, dealers said.</p>
<p>Turnover in excess of 590,000 shares of PTCL was recorded in early trade.</p>
<p>&quot;PTCL price soared because its revenue would increase if telephone line rent is doubled,&quot; dealer Shakil Anwar said. &quot;The GDR (Global Depositary Receipt) of PTCL is also up abroad.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192.</p>
</text>
